{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1362644-aberrant-campaign-concept","id":1362644,"title":"Aberrant campaign concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-22T07:53:58-08:00","id":1362644,"title":"Aberrant campaign concept","content":"So I had an idea early on when I was reading the previews for Aberrant and I thought I'd share it here. The elevator pitch is this:<br /> <br /> <b>What if Magneto's Brotherhood of Mutants had a PR team?</b><br /> <br /> The PCs would work for a highly influential Terat who believes that though Nova's <i>should</i> be free to plot their own destinies without limitations, he knows that complete freedom is fundamentally impossible for the simple fact that baselines and Nova's have to share the planet with each other and baselines will strike out if Nova's go too far. So his goal is to make the world acknowledge Nova's as a nation unto themselves, with all the independence and autonomy such implies, answerable only to authority they themselves decide upon. He sponsors the PCs to basically be superheroes, demystifying the Teragen and making them look good.<br /> <br /> The campaign would go through the characters joining him, doing some superhero stuff and winning people around to the cause, navigating Teragen politics with regard to Terats who are against their ideals, and if the players manage to pull off getting Nova's granted independence, they would essentially become the Novas police force and the focus would shift to primarily investigating Nova crimes and navigating the friction and politics of actually being a nation unto themselves.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, comments and suggestions are all welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T07:59:38-08:00","id":1362649,"title":"","content":"That sounds amazing!! Maybe you could do a storyline leading up to the Night of Long Knives, where Divis Mal sits back and watches while your PCs try and stop the Apostle and Tarik ibn'Mahmoud from seizing control of the Teragen and killing the less radical Pantheon members.<br /> <br /> I love your idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (insert heart emoji; I'm not on my phone rn)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T08:00:10-08:00","id":1362650,"title":"","content":"Check out the Mathematician. He could be your players' patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T08:41:06-08:00","id":1362660,"title":"","content":"Mathematician would be on board sure, but Orzaiz seems like he'd be fully on board as well. He's basically parading around his novadom like a celebrity anyway, funding a bunch of terat &quot;superheroes&quot; seems like a great way to advance his causes along with theirs. Narcosis might be all over this too (for not quite the right reasons).<br /> <br /> Of course, that 